---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site, url } from '../data/site';
const updated = '17 October 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="FinvestLens privacy policy. There is no account, no analytics and no server of ours — your book is a file you keep."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lead={`Last updated ${updated}`} />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <div
      class="mb-12 rounded-2xl border border-brand-200 bg-brand-50/60 p-6 dark:border-brand-800/60 dark:bg-brand-900/20"
    >
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-800 dark:text-ink-100">
        <strong>The short version.</strong> FinvestLens has no account to sign up for,
        no analytics, and no server of ours for your data to reach. Your book is a
        file you keep — on your device, or in your own iCloud Drive or Box account.
        We never see it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-doc">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        FinvestLens is published by <a href={site.publisher.url}>{site.publisher.legalName}</a>
        (“we”, “us”). For anything in this policy, write to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Nothing.</strong> We operate no servers for FinvestLens, run no
        analytics or crash reporting, use no advertising or tracking SDKs, and have
        no way to identify you. The app’s privacy manifest declares no collected data
        types and no tracking domains.
      </p>

      <h2>Where your financial data lives</h2>
      <p>
        Your book is a single file you choose the location of — local disk, iCloud
        Drive, a network share, or your own Box account. It is read and written by
        the app on your device, and goes only where you chose to keep it. Attachments
        you link are likewise files on your storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you keep your book in iCloud Drive, it syncs between <em>your own</em>
        devices through your Apple Account, under Apple’s terms and encryption. That
        is a transfer between you and Apple; it does not involve us.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you keep your book in your own Box account, the app keeps a copy on your
        device while you work on it and sends it back to Box when you save with ⌘S,
        close the book, switch books or quit (on iPhone and iPad, also when you leave
        the app). A version saved by another of your devices is never replaced: you are
        asked what to keep. That is a transfer between you and Box, under Box’s terms;
        it does not involve us.
      </p>

      <h2>Apple Intelligence and document reading</h2>
      <p>
        Smart Import, categorisation suggestions, budget proposals and report
        commentary are produced by Apple Intelligence — on your device, or, where
        Apple offers it and you allow it, on Apple’s Private Cloud Compute (below).
        You can use a model of your own instead, which runs on your device; we
        provide no model and download none. The contents of the documents you point
        the app at are never sent to us.
      </p>

      <h2>Network requests the app can make</h2>
      <p>
        FinvestLens contacts a network service in three situations, all started by you.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Prices and company data.</strong> When you update prices, look up a
        security or fetch a company’s details, the app asks the provider you chose:
        Yahoo Finance, Stooq, EODHD (<code>eodhd.com</code>), Alpha Vantage
        (<code>alphavantage.co</code>), Finnhub (<code>finnhub.io</code>), Twelve Data
        (<code>twelvedata.com</code>), FIIG (bond prices) or Wilson Asset Management (its
        own funds’ unit prices). The request carries the ticker, ISIN or fund name —
        never an amount, a balance or anything else from your book — and goes from your
        device straight to that provider, under its own privacy policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Your own Box account.</strong> If you connect a Box account, the app
        signs you in on Box’s own page and then reads and writes the book files you
        choose there — with Open from Box…, and when you save as described above —
        directly between your device and Box. We never see your Box credentials or your
        files.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Apple’s Private Cloud Compute.</strong> Where it is available,
        FinvestLens can use Apple’s Private Cloud Compute. Match Attachments, Categorise
        from Attachment and Split from Invoice send the documents they read; Smart Import
        sends the invoices and dividend statements it finds; and commentary on reports
        and reviews, budget suggestions and the forecast outlook send the figures they
        are written from. Apple states that data processed by Private Cloud Compute is
        not stored or made accessible to Apple. The first time a command would use it,
        the app asks you; you can keep everything on your device instead, and change
        your answer at any time in Settings ▸ Apple Intelligence. A PDF imported as a
        bank statement is always read on your device, and Auto-Categorise and an
        import’s category suggestions always run on it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you do none of these, the app makes no network requests at all. It works
        entirely offline.
      </p>

      <h2>API keys and credentials</h2>
      <p>
        Keys for the keyed price providers, and the client secret and sign-in tokens
        of your Box app, are stored in the Keychain on the device you enter them on.
        They are never written into your book file and are never transmitted anywhere
        except to the service they belong to.
      </p>

      <h2>Local authentication</h2>
      <p>
        Where the app asks for Touch ID or your password — to open a protected book,
        or to reach Emergency Records — that check is performed by macOS. FinvestLens
        receives only a yes or no. It never sees your password or biometric data.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        FinvestLens is a general-purpose accounting application, not directed at
        children, and collects no data from anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Rights of access, correction, deletion and portability apply to data a
        publisher holds about you. We hold none. Your own data is in your own file:
        you can read it, change it, export it to GnuCash XML or a Ledger journal, or
        delete the file, all without asking us.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the revised version will be published on this page
        with a new date. Material changes will also be noted in the release notes.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a> ·
        <a href={url('/support/')}>Support</a> ·
        <a href={site.publisher.url}>{site.publisher.legalName}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
